cman: pin the mcp SDK below 2.0

server.py declares its PEP 723 inline dependency as `mcp>=1.0` with no upper
bound, so `uv run --script` resolves the newest release. mcp 2.0.0 dropped the
`mcp.server.fastmcp` module, which server.py imports, so every cman MCP tool
call fails at startup with:

    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mcp.server.fastmcp'

Verified 2026-08-01: the module is present in mcp 1.9.4 / 1.12.0 / 1.15.0 /
1.20.0 and absent in 2.0.0. Pinning `<2` makes the server start again.

Affects every released version of cman up to v1.6.0 (in v1.6.0 the import moved
into main(), but it is the same import and the same failure). No upstream issue
exists for this as of 2026-08-01 — laiso/cman has only #3 (closed, unrelated).
Drop this patch once upstream pins the dependency or migrates to the standalone
`fastmcp` package.

Applied by install.sh against every ~/.claude/plugins/cache/cman/cman/*/server.py.

--- a/server.py
+++ b/server.py
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 # /// script
-# dependencies = ["mcp>=1.0"]
+# dependencies = ["mcp>=1.0,<2"]
 # ///
